ame","summary":"{\n  \"name\": \"]]\",\n  \"rows\": 5,\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"column\": \"TotalWorkingYears\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 1,\n        \"min\": 6,\n        \"max\": 10,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          10,\n          6,\n          8\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"NumCompaniesWorked\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 3,\n        \"min\": 1,\n        \"max\": 9,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          1,\n          9,\n          8\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"years_per_company\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 2.0464120966061072,\n        \"min\": 0.6,\n        \"max\": 5.0,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 5,\n        \"samples\": [\n          5.0,\n          0.6,\n          1.0\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Age\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 8,\n        \"min\": 27,\n        \"max\": 49,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 5,\n        \"samples\": [\n          49,\n          27,\n          37\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"age_band\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"category\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 3,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"40-49\",\n          \"30-39\",\n          \"18-29\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Verify encoding, new features and missing values\n","\n","print(\"BusinessTravel values:\")\n","print(df_clean[\"BusinessTravel\"].value_counts(dropna=False))\n","\n","print(\"\\nOverTime values:\")\n","print(df_clean[\"OverTime\"].value_counts(dropna=False))\n","\n","print(\"\\nAttrition values:\")\n","print(df_clean[\"Attrition\"].value_counts(dropna=False))\n","\n","print(\"\\nAge bands:\")\n","print(df_clean[\"age_band\"].value_counts(dropna=False))\n","\n","print(\"\\nMissing values after transformation:\")\n","print(df_clean.isnull().sum()[df_clean.isnull().sum() > 0])\n","\n","print(\"\\nNew features:\")\n","display(df_clean[[\n","    \"TotalWorkingYears\",\n","    \"NumCompaniesWorked\",\n","    \"years_per_company\",\n","    \"Age\",\n","    \"age_band\"\n","]].head())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"-wJVfln1TZDt"},"source":["Why BusinessTravel is ordinal encoded but JobRole is one-hot encoded\n","\n","BusinessTravel is ordinal because its categories have a meaningful order based on travel frequency: Non-Travel, Travel_Rarely and Travel_Frequently. Therefore, numerical values 0, 1 and 2 can represent this order. JobRole is nominal because its categories represent different job positions without a natural ranking. One-hot encoding is therefore appropriate because it represents each job role separately without suggesting an artificial order."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"metadata":{"id":"dCc0SQkETZ_-","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607864304,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":157,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"31bbc0da-91a8-44a0-d5f0-b4af7a1643cf"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Saved successfully to: /content/drive/MyDrive/CSC4110_G09/data/clean_hr.csv\n"]}],"source":["# Save the transformed dataset for subsequent machine learning tasks\n","\n","df_clean.to_csv(DATA_DIR / \"clean_hr.csv\", index=False)\n","\n","print(\"Saved successfully to:\", DATA_DIR / \"clean_hr.csv\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"4tVCFrJ_T7tr"},"source":["Create the five EDA charts"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Yud3Lts3VF5_"},"source":["Histogram of MonthlyIncome"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"metadata":{"id":"Ef1tVK9rVGin","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":189},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607865586,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":1279,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"b841d762-dcaa-49e7-d047-5b17525b0a26"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Chart 1: Display the distribution of monthly income\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n","\n","sns.histplot(\n","    data=df_clean,\n","    x=\"MonthlyIncome\",\n","    bins=30,\n","    kde=True\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Distribution of Monthly Income\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Monthly Income\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Number of Employees\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"hist_target.png\", dpi=300)\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"jaM91caDVQRt"},"source":["Box plot of YearsAtCompany"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"metadata":{"id":"S-3pUkEIVQ8d","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":189},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607866095,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":515,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"fce43aa0-e246-4e89-a353-406321d5729e"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Chart 2: Display the distribution of years at the company\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n","\n","sns.boxplot(\n","    data=df_clean,\n","    x=\"YearsAtCompany\"\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Box Plot of Years at Company\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Years at Company\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"box_feature.png\", dpi=300)\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"6jNC9mliVYBv"},"source":["Bar chart of Attrition"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"metadata":{"id":"PX8QYBAPVYkq","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":308},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607866738,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":642,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"0544e547-2ecd-48e6-a78d-05c585441605"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 700x500 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Attrition\n","No     1233\n","Yes     237\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n"]}],"source":["# Chart 3: Display the number of employees who left or stayed\n","\n","attrition_counts = (\n","    df_clean[\"Attrition\"]\n","    .map({0: \"No\", 1: \"Yes\"})\n","    .value_counts()\n","    .reindex([\"No\", \"Yes\"])\n",")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(7, 5))\n","\n","sns.barplot(\n","    x=attrition_counts.index,\n","    y=attrition_counts.values\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Employee Attrition Distribution\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Attrition\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Number of Employees\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"bar_class.png\", dpi=300)\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(attrition_counts)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"stK41D1sVoq_"},"source":["**Scatter plot of the best numeric predictor against MonthlyIncome**\n","\n","Purpose: Shows the relationship between the numeric feature most strongly correlated with MonthlyIncome and employees' monthly incomes.\n","\n","First, identify the strongest numeric predictor using the original cleaned dataset:"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"o82sW39LVpxD","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607866816,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":75,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"2dcabb26-ef09-4d16-9bee-30796a9d2445"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Best numeric predictor: JobLevel\n","Correlation: 0.9502999134798473\n"]}],"source":["# Chart 4: Identify the strongest numeric predictor of MonthlyIncome\n","\n","numeric_df = df_stage1.select_dtypes(include=np.number)\n","\n","correlations = (\n","    numeric_df.corr()[\"MonthlyIncome\"]\n","    .drop(\"MonthlyIncome\")\n","    .dropna()\n",")\n","\n","best_feature = correlations.abs().idxmax()\n","\n","print(\"Best numeric predictor:\", best_feature)\n","print(\"Correlation:\", correlations[best_feature])"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":189},"id":"QDedyg6CWAj8","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607867776,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":956,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"0515697a-3c8c-4147-b783-24096e4bed13"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Plot the relationship between the best predictor and MonthlyIncome\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n","\n","sns.scatterplot(\n","    data=df_stage1,\n","    x=best_feature,\n","    y=\"MonthlyIncome\",\n","    alpha=0.6\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(f\"{best_feature} vs Monthly Income\")\n","plt.xlabel(best_feature)\n","plt.ylabel(\"Monthly Income\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"scatter_best.png\", dpi=300)\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"vkQR5u-PWI7S"},"source":["**Correlation heatmap**\n","\n","Purpose: Displays correlations between numeric variables. It helps identify variables that have strong positive or negative relationships."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":15,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":277},"id":"A93bmHrnWRKB","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607874446,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":6610,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"eec5b8e8-a18e-45f8-86bb-441a8653ad8f"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1800x1400 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Chart 5: Display correlations between numeric variables\n","\n","numeric_data = df_clean.select_dtypes(include=np.number)\n","\n","correlation_matrix = numeric_data.corr()\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(18, 14))\n","\n","sns.heatmap(\n","    correlation_matrix,\n","    cmap=\"coolwarm\",\n","    center=0,\n","    annot=False,\n","    linewidths=0.3\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Correlation Heatmap of Numeric Features\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"corr_heatmap.png\", dpi=300)\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":16,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"_yly_TwnWXvq","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607874470,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":20,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"1fd1d4c7-18f4-4851-8563-126171a96546"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["hist_target.png : Saved\n","box_feature.png : Saved\n","bar_class.png : Saved\n","scatter_best.png : Saved\n","corr_heatmap.png : Saved\n"]}],"source":["# Verify that all five EDA charts have been saved\n","\n","chart_files = [\n","    \"hist_target.png\",\n","    \"box_feature.png\",\n","    \"bar_class.png\",\n","    \"scatter_best.png\",\n","    \"corr_heatmap.png\"\n","]\n","\n","for filename in chart_files:\n","    file_path = OUTPUT_DIR / filename\n","    print(filename, \":\", \"Saved\" if file_path.exists() else \"Missing\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"zJ90bfy-Wx53"},"source":["Min-Max Scaling and Standard Scaling"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":17,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"LDgPumd9XBgb","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607874519,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":44,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"5becb1c9-ea1c-4a82-cb4d-55681faf3c34"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Scaling libraries imported successfully.\n"]}],"source":["# Import scaling techniques from scikit-learn\n","\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler, StandardScaler\n","\n","print(\"Scaling libraries imported successfully.\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":244},"id":"oYH7oyoxNtGd","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607874572,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":50,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"9032aec4-27c5-4001-a3e3-317b6859f605"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["First five observations: TotalWorkingYears scaling comparison\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["   Original  Min_Max_Scaled  Standard_Scaled\n","0         8           0.200        -0.421642\n","1        10           0.250        -0.164511\n","2         7           0.175        -0.550208\n","3         8           0.200        -0.421642\n","4         6           0.150        -0.678774"],"text/html":["\n","  <div id=\"df-37b20f90-b1c6-49e9-8b22-0746827adf91\" class=\"colab-df-container\">\n","    <div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Original</th>\n","      <th>Min_Max_Scaled</th>\n","      <th>Standard_Scaled</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <