"      }\n","\n","      .colab-df-generate:hover {\n","        background-color: #E2EBFA;\n","        box-shadow: 0px 1px 2px rgba(60, 64, 67, 0.3), 0px 1px 3px 1px rgba(60, 64, 67, 0.15);\n","        fill: #174EA6;\n","      }\n","\n","      [theme=dark] .colab-df-generate {\n","        background-color: #3B4455;\n","        fill: #D2E3FC;\n","      }\n","\n","      [theme=dark] .colab-df-generate:hover {\n","        background-color: #434B5C;\n","        box-shadow: 0px 1px 3px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);\n","        filter: drop-shadow(0px 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3));\n","        fill: #FFFFFF;\n","      }\n","    </style>\n","    <button class=\"colab-df-generate\" onclick=\"generateWithVariable('scaling_comparison')\"\n","            title=\"Generate code using this dataframe.\"\n","            style=\"display:none;\">\n","\n","  <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"24px\"viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n","       width=\"24px\">\n","    <path d=\"M7,19H8.4L18.45,9,17,7.55,7,17.6ZM5,21V16.75L18.45,3.32a2,2,0,0,1,2.83,0l1.4,1.43a1.91,1.91,0,0,1,.58,1.4,1.91,1.91,0,0,1-.58,1.4L9.25,21ZM18.45,9,17,7.55Zm-12,3A5.31,5.31,0,0,0,4.9,8.1,5.31,5.31,0,0,0,1,6.5,5.31,5.31,0,0,0,4.9,4.9,5.31,5.31,0,0,0,6.5,1,5.31,5.31,0,0,0,8.1,4.9,5.31,5.31,0,0,0,12,6.5,5.46,5.46,0,0,0,6.5,12Z\"/>\n","  </svg>\n","    </button>\n","    <script>\n","      (() => {\n","      const buttonEl =\n","        document.querySelector('#id_2a3a47c1-b0de-4a10-97f6-5bbd6f743ee1 button.colab-df-generate');\n","      buttonEl.style.display =\n","        google.colab.kernel.accessAllowed ? 'block' : 'none';\n","\n","      buttonEl.onclick = () => {\n","        google.colab.notebook.generateWithVariable('scaling_comparison');\n","      }\n","      })();\n","    </script>\n","  </div>\n","\n","    </div>\n","  </div>\n"],"application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json":{"type":"dataframe","variable_name":"scaling_comparison","summary":"{\n  \"name\": \"scaling_comparison\",\n  \"rows\": 5,\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Original\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 1,\n        \"min\": 6,\n        \"max\": 10,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          10,\n          6,\n          8\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Min_Max_Scaled\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.037080992435478306,\n        \"min\": 0.15000000000000002,\n        \"max\": 0.25,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0.25,\n          0.15000000000000002,\n          0.2\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Standard_Scaled\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.19069349586460604,\n        \"min\": -0.678773515728442,\n        \"max\": -0.16451140099023315,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          -0.16451140099023315,\n          -0.678773515728442,\n          -0.42164245835933756\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Demonstrate Min-Max and Standard scaling on TotalWorkingYears\n","\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler, StandardScaler\n","import pandas as pd\n","\n","# Select TotalWorkingYears\n","years = df_clean[[\"TotalWorkingYears\"]]\n","\n","# Apply Min-Max scaling\n","minmax_scaler = MinMaxScaler()\n","minmax_values = minmax_scaler.fit_transform(years)\n","\n","# Apply Standard scaling\n","standard_scaler = StandardScaler()\n","standard_values = standard_scaler.fit_transform(years)\n","\n","# Create comparison table\n","scaling_comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n","    \"Original\": years[\"TotalWorkingYears\"].head(5).values,\n","    \"Min_Max_Scaled\": minmax_values[:5].flatten(),\n","    \"Standard_Scaled\": standard_values[:5].flatten()\n","})\n","\n","# Display results\n","print(\"First five observations: TotalWorkingYears scaling comparison\")\n","display(scaling_comparison)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"StCheXE5XfBi"},"source":["**Min-Max Scaling:** This technique transforms values into a specified range, usually between 0 and 1. It is useful when features need to have the same bounded range, particularly for algorithms sensitive to feature magnitude.\n","\n","Standard Scaling: This technique transforms values so that the feature has a mean of approximately 0 and a standard deviation of approximately 1. It is useful for algorithms that work better when numerical features are standardised.\n","\n","Difference: Min-Max Scaling produces values within a fixed range, while Standard Scaling centres values around zero without restricting them to a fixed range."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"DyTogZuZZtiO"},"source":["**Train-Test Split**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"3xspdO6LZubJ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607874611,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":36,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"d4a1badc-cddf-423f-877e-e7f331d23914"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Features shape: (1470, 47)\n","Target shape: (1470,)\n","\n","Feature columns:\n","['Age', 'BusinessTravel', 'DailyRate', 'DistanceFromHome', 'Education', 'EnvironmentSatisfaction', 'HourlyRate', 'JobInvolvement', 'JobSatisfaction', 'MonthlyRate', 'NumCompaniesWorked', 'OverTime', 'PercentSalaryHike', 'PerformanceRating', 'RelationshipSatisfaction', 'StockOptionLevel', 'TotalWorkingYears', 'TrainingTimesLastYear', 'WorkLifeBalance', 'YearsAtCompany', 'YearsInCurrentRole', 'YearsSinceLastPromotion', 'YearsWithCurrManager', 'Department_Human Resources', 'Department_Research & Development', 'Department_Sales', 'EducationField_Human Resources', 'EducationField_Life Sciences', 'EducationField_Marketing', 'EducationField_Medical', 'EducationField_Other', 'EducationField_Technical Degree', 'JobRole_Healthcare Representative', 'JobRole_Human Resources', 'JobRole_Laboratory Technician', 'JobRole_Manager', 'JobRole_Manufacturing Director', 'JobRole_Research Director', 'JobRole_Research Scientist', 'JobRole_Sales Executive', 'JobRole_Sales Representative', 'MaritalStatus_Divorced', 'MaritalStatus_Married', 'MaritalStatus_Single', 'Gender_Female', 'Gender_Male', 'years_per_company']\n"]}],"source":["# Separate predictors and regression target\n","\n","target_column = \"MonthlyIncome\"\n","\n","# Exclude target, Attrition, JobLevel and age_band from predictors\n","excluded_columns = [\n","    \"MonthlyIncome\",\n","    \"Attrition\",\n","    \"JobLevel\",\n","    \"age_band\"\n","]\n","\n","X = df_clean.drop(columns=excluded_columns)\n","y = df_clean[target_column]\n","\n","print(\"Features shape:\", X.shape)\n","print(\"Target shape:\", y.shape)\n","print(\"\\nFeature columns:\")\n","print(X.columns.tolist())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"wW9px0SvagE9","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607874625,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":11,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"d47089ea-6cc6-4602-f5e3-64c02599e04b"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Training features: (1176, 47)\n","Testing features: (294, 47)\n","Training target: (1176,)\n","Testing target: (294,)\n"]}],"source":["# Split the dataset into training and testing sets\n","\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n","\n","X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n","    X,\n","    y,\n","    test_size=0.20,\n","    random_state=42,\n","    stratify=df_clean[\"Attrition\"]\n",")\n","\n","print(\"Training features:\", X_train.shape)\n","print(\"Testing features:\", X_test.shape)\n","print(\"Training target:\", y_train.shape)\n","print(\"Testing target:\", y_test.shape)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"mg30-4Y5ao_-"},"source":["**Scaling the features correctly**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"zsAEI2QoamLA","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1795607874642,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":15,"user":{"displayName":"Owiye Sylvia","userId":"11193821584558389181"}},"outputId":"5bca5d15-ae18-480a-8a5b-05acabc52429"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Training data scaled: (1176, 47)\n","Testing data scaled: (294, 47)\n","\n","Scaler fitted on training data only.\n"]}],"source":["# Fit the scaler on training data only to prevent data leakage\n","\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n","\n","scaler = StandardScaler()\n","\n","X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n","X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n","\n","print(\"Training data scaled:\", X_train_scaled.shape)\n","print(\"Testing data scaled:\", X_test_scaled.shape)\n","print(\"\\nScaler fitted on training data only.\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"trASW0skaxyX"},"source":["**Train-Test Split and Data Scaling**\n","\n","The dataset was divided into training and testing sets using an 80:20 ratio. The training set contains 1,176 observations, while the testing set contains 294 observations. The split was performed using random_state=42 to ensure reproducibility and stratified using Attrition to maintain a similar distribution of employees who left and those who stayed. StandardScaler was fitted only on the training data and subsequently used to transform both the training and testing features. This approach prevents data leakage and ensures a fair evaluation of the models on unseen data."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"pVjSwNqWbQjq"},"source":["### **Exploratory Data Analysis Findings**\n","\n","The exploratory data analysis was conducted to understand the distribution of employee monthly income, identify potential outliers, examine employee attrition, and explore relationships between numerical variables. The MonthlyIncome histogram shows the distribution of employee salaries and helps identify income concentration and variation. The YearsAtCompany box plot illustrates the spread of employees' tenure and highlights potential outliers. The Attrition bar chart reveals an imbalance between employees who stayed and those who left the organization, with 1,233 employees staying and 237 leaving. The scatter plot explores the relationship between the strongest numerical predictor and MonthlyIncome, while the correlation heatmap provides an overview of relationships among numerical features. These findings help guide feature selection, data preparation, and subsequent model development."]}],"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[]},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0}